{"name":"Spinach Banana Smoothie","hex":"#aaaa55","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spinach","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any member of species Spinacia oleracea of edible plants, or its leaves.","Any of numerous plants, or their leaves, which are used for greens in the same way Spinacia oleracea is or resemble it in some way."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spinach"},{"term":"banana","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The elongated curved tropical fruit of a banana plant, which grows in bunches and has a creamy flesh and a smooth skin. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","In particular, the sweet, yellow fruit of the Cavendish banana cultivar, which may be eaten raw, as distinct from e.g. a plantain for cooking."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Curved like a banana, especially of a ball in flight."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/banana"},{"term":"smoothie","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A smooth-talking person.","A drink made from whole fruit, thus thicker than fruit juice."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smoothie"}],"entries":[{"title":"Smoothie","blocks":[{"text":"A smoothie is a beverage made by puréeing ingredients in a blender. A smoothie commonly has a liquid base, such as fruit juice, milk, yogurt, or ice cream. Other ingredients may be added, including fruits, vegetables, non-dairy milk, crushed ice, spices, herbs, sweetener, whey powder, or nutritional supplements."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Kiwi_Smoothie.jpg/330px-Kiwi_Smoothie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smoothie","wikidata":"Q13290"},{"title":"Spinach","blocks":[{"text":"Spinach is a leafy green flowering plant native to Central and Western Asia. It is of the order Caryophyllales, family Amaranthaceae, subfamily Chenopodioideae. Its leaves are a common vegetable consumed either fresh, cooked or after storage. The taste differs considerably between cooked and raw: the high oxalate content may be reduced by blanching."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Spinacia_oleracea_Spinazie_bloeiend.jpg/330px-Spinacia_oleracea_Spinazie_bloeiend.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spinach","wikidata":"Q81464"},{"title":"Banana","blocks":[{"text":"A banana is an elongated, edible fruit that is botanically a berry produced by several kinds of large treelike herbaceous flowering plants in the genus Musa. In some countries, cooking bananas are called plantains, distinguishing them from dessert bananas. The fruit is variable in size, color and firmness, but is usually elongated and curved, with soft flesh rich in starch covered with a peel, which may have a variety of colors when ripe. It grows upward in clusters near the top of the plant. Almost all modern edible seedless (parthenocarp) cultivated bananas come from two wild species – Musa acuminata and Musa balbisiana, or their hybrids."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Bananavarieties.jpg/330px-Bananavarieties.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banana","wikidata":"Q503"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Fruit_smoothie_%288475314736%29.png/500px-Fruit_smoothie_%288475314736%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Fruit_smoothie_%288475314736%29.png/1280px-Fruit_smoothie_%288475314736%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Fruit_smoothie_%288475314736%29.png/500px-Fruit_smoothie_%288475314736%29.png?utm_source=en.wi